# `npx storybook tools` runs the docgen of the component manifest: a
# TypeScript program of the whole app. It needs more than the default heap of
# about 4 GB. With less, the docgen stops at its timeout, and
# `storybook tools docs list` silently drops the docs of most components.
# npx applies this value to each command that starts in apps/ui; it replaces a
# NODE_OPTIONS of the shell. pnpm 11 reads only auth and registry settings from
# .npmrc, so no pnpm command applies it. Thus the `typecheck`, `storybook` and
# `build-storybook` scripts add the same heap to NODE_OPTIONS themselves.
node-options=--max-old-space-size=6144
